From d4f306e259f9cd1347ff50518ba784af63adc34a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Hartkopp <socketcan@hartkopp.net>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:33:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/34] can: isotp: check the data length of the last CF

A CF shorter than LL_DL is only allowed as last CF. The check only
tested whether the remaining PDU data would fit into a full CF. So a
short CF with less than the remaining bytes was accepted and the
reception continued with further CFs.

Require the short CF to contain all remaining bytes. Padding is still
possible as it only increases datalen. isotp_rcv() ensures datalen >=
ae + N_PCI_SZ, so the right side can not underflow.

Fixes: e057dd3fc20f ("can: add ISO 15765-2:2016 transport protocol")
Signed-off-by: Oliver Hartkopp <socketcan@hartkopp.net>
---
 net/can/isotp/protocolrx.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/can/isotp/protocolrx.c b/net/can/isotp/protocolrx.c
index 794f2b9..4d9063f 100644
--- a/net/can/isotp/protocolrx.c
+++ b/net/can/isotp/protocolrx.c
@@ -361,8 +361,10 @@ static void isotp_rcv_cf(struct sock *sk, u8 *data, unsigned int datalen,
 
 	/* CFs have usually the LL_DL length */
 	if (datalen < so->rx.ll_dl) {
-		/* this is only allowed for the last CF */
-		if (so->rx.len - so->rx.idx > so->rx.ll_dl - ae - N_PCI_SZ)
+		/* only the last CF may be shorter: it has to contain
+		 * all remaining bytes of the PDU (plus optional padding)
+		 */
+		if (so->rx.len - so->rx.idx > datalen - ae - N_PCI_SZ)
 			return;
 	}
 
